WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — rce-jepa (90s) Narrator Jyothi

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.871
First, instead of guessing raw code word by word,

2
00:00:03.871 --> 00:00:08.073
small models predict compact summaries of program meaning.

3
00:00:08.573 --> 00:00:12.742
Second, any AI model may propose a candidate program,

4
00:00:12.742 --> 00:00:16.438
but a fast, strict checker decides what passes.

5
00:00:16.938 --> 00:00:22.675
Third, checking uses seventeen hundred times less energy than generating,

6
00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:25.662
and saved fixes slash big model calls.

7
00:00:26.162 --> 00:00:32.006
Ordinary source files bury real program logic under formatting, imports, and language

8
00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:39.636
quirks. Across one hundred eighty-five hand-written programs, Reality Code Engine blueprints shrink description

9
00:00:39.636 --> 00:00:45.480
length more than nine times, giving small neural models a compact, noise-free target.

10
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:53.206
First, deterministic rules close one hundred eleven of one hundred fifty-one real-history tasks

11
00:00:53.206 --> 00:01:01.345
with zero AI calls. Second, tiny six-to-eight-million-parameter meaning predictors and energy scorers solve

12
00:01:01.345 --> 00:01:07.659
repairs under half a joule. Third, only remaining open tasks call a frontier model.

13
00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:14.167
Given up to five turns of exact checker diagnostics and public library headers, Claude

14
00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:20.386
Opus and Sonnet close all forty hard residual tasks with zero contradictions. Zero fuzzed

15
00:01:20.386 --> 00:01:27.163
bugs slip past the gate, and saved lookup cuts recurring frontier runs sixteen-point-seven times.

16
00:01:27.663 --> 00:01:34.978
When an outside stochastic repair step hit two point five percent against its pre-registered two percent ceiling,

17
00:01:34.978 --> 00:01:38.150
our harness honestly kept it in observation mode.
